    day-201 counter repair invisible in the census for a whole session (2 and 0 before it,
    2 and 0 after). The day-201 lesson states the required form of the number: "measure the
    base rate, then restrict it by every condition on the path from the entry point to the
    changed line, and quote it as a fraction over THAT set". So:

      N -- hunks the classifier returned WEAKENED for, i.e. the population the payoff gate
           admits. It equals the report's own `WEAKENED ..... N` line BY CONSTRUCTION and a
           self-test pins the two together, so the denominator can never describe a
           population the verdict counts disagree with.
      M -- those of the N whose REMOVED side carries a register literal (the day-201
           `dense-or-joined` pair, reused rather than re-spelled).
      K -- the subset of M whose removed register literal is visible ONLY on the join --
           the day-201 rustfmt split. K == 0 over an M > 0 denominator is the honest reading
           this line exists to make sayable.

    REMOVED SIDE ONLY, and the limit is stated rather than left to be discovered: the added
    side is deliberately out of scope because `count_register_payoff`'s WEAKENED gate never
    looks at added lines either. `M` and `register-lines-only` are DISJOINT by construction
    -- that counter skips every hunk that produced a finding, and every hunk counted here
    produced one.
    """
    n = m = k = 0
    for f, h in _hunk_by_finding(findings, hunks):
        if f.verdict != WEAKENED:
            continue
        n += 1
        if not hunk_carries_shape(
            h.removed, REGISTER_LITERAL_RE, REGISTER_LITERAL_JOINED_RE
        ):
            continue
        m += 1
        if not any(REGISTER_LITERAL_RE.search(ln) for ln in h.removed):
            k += 1
    return n, m, k
```

